# Airfoil-Shaped Landing Gear

This block creates a printable two-wheel landing gear bracket with struts, fastener holes, and a curved mounting plate conforming to the fuselage belly. It has an airfoil profile to reduce drag since it is non-retractable. It also outputs the fastener hole bodies to be later subtracted from the fuselage.

## Installation

Clone this repo or copy the package folder into your nTop workspace:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/nTopology/Utilities-community.git
```

The package lives at `packages/natalie-scala/airfoil-shaped-landing-gear/`.

## Usage

1. Open the provided `.ntop` file in nTop 4.26+.
2. Specify input dimensions and positions and drop in fuselage block.
3. Create variables for each body in output implicit body list (bracket, fastener holes, axle).
4. Offset bracket body and boolean subtract from fuselage to create a recess with tolerance in the fuselage belly for the curved mounting plate.
5. Boolean subtract fastener holes from fuselage.

## Inputs & outputs

| Name | Type | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| `Bracket Position` | Vector | Required. |
| `Horizontal Bar Length` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Diagonal Length` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Diagonal Angle` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Wheel Face Length` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `NACA 4-digit code` | Code | Required. |
| `Axle Hole Radius` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Fuselage` | Implicit Body | Required. |
| `Curved Plate Thickness` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Curved Plate Height` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Curved Plate Length` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Blend` | Scalar | Required. |
| `Fastener Shaft Diameter` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Fastener Spacing` | Vector| Required. |
| `Fastener Head Diameter` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Fastener Hole Height` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Fastener Head Depth` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `Fastener Hole Bottom` | Unit Length | Required. |
| `output_1` | Implicit Body List | Main result. |

